<title>UK: CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP CLOSES/RESULTS.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP CLOSES/RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Close of play scores on and</p>
<p>results on the third day of four-day English County Championship</p>
<p>cricket matches on Saturday:</p>
<p>At Cardiff: Middlesex beat Glamorgan by an innings and seven</p>
<p>runs. Glamorgan 281 and 31 in 16 overs (J.Hewitt 6-14, A.Fraser</p>
<p>4-17). Middlesex 319. Middlesex 23 points Glamorgan 6.</p>
<p>At Basingstoke: Hampshire beat Somerset by nine runs.</p>
<p>Hampshire 204 and 189. Somerset 159 and 225 (K.Parsons 74,</p>
<p>P.Holloway 59; K.James 8-49). Hampshire 21 points Somerset 4.</p>
<p>At Hove: Essex beat Sussex by ten wickets. Sussex 140 and</p>
<p>356 (A.Cowan 4-78). Essex 384 and 115-0 (P.Prichard 54 not out,</p>
<p>G.Gooch 51 not out). Essex 24 points Sussex 4.</p>
<p>At The Oval: Surrey 549 and 153 (C.Silverwood 5-49).</p>
<p>Yorkshire 387 (D.Lehmann 100, R.Blakey 53 not out; A.Hollioake</p>
<p>4-22) and 19-0.</p>
<p>At Bristol: Worcestershire 250 and 350-4 declared (G.Hick</p>
<p>137, T.Curtis 137). Gloucestershire 229 and 9-1.</p>
<p>At Edgbaston: Derbyshire 200. Warwickshire 321-7 (T.Penney</p>
<p>72 not).</p>
<p>At Old Trafford: Kent 373 and 81-4. Lancashire 285 (G.Lloyd</p>
<p>122; P.Strang 7-118).</p>
</text>
